heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or before one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written earlier, by ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its written place:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to throw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","text":"Running Systems at the Same Time","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two systems ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"conflict","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on how they happen to be written. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" lists those pairs, so a test can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/runIf(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runIf(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/runif(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns this schedule with each of its systems run only when a condition holds."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"runIf(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runIf","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"typeIdentifier","pre